      "index": 0,
      "type": "text",
      "weight": 0.4,
      "score": 34,
      "reasoning": "This is an objective quantitative criterion. The report reproduces several published central values for comparison, but its own results are notably weaker: −6226 rather than −6542 Gt, 28% rather than 36% acceleration, and −435 Gt rather than the record −548 Gt in 2023; it also omits the key published uncertainties and does not quantify the 18% Greenland and >2× Antarctic comparisons. The simplified, benchmark-informed methodology and acknowledged underestimated uncertainties further limit validity."
     },
     {
      "index": 1,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.1,
      "score": 36,
      "reasoning": "This is Mode A because the criterion requires specific regional percentages and quantitative mass-change rates. The contribution plot reproduces the main absolute shares reasonably well—Alaska ≈23%, combined Canadian Arctic ≈21%, Greenland periphery ≈13%, and Southern Andes ≈9–10%—but the required relative losses versus 2000 ice volume (−39%, −35%, etc.) are not calculated or visualized, and Canada must be manually summed across two regions."
     },
     {
      "index": 2,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.2,
      "score": 18,
      "reasoning": "Mode A. The report attempts a quantitative method comparison, but its main plot merges glaciological, DEM, and hybrid data, uses an unsuitable compressed Gt/yr scale, omits method uncertainties and observation periods, and does not reproduce the target’s regional method-by-method estimates. It also fails to report the key DEM-relative differences (0.08 ± 0.08, 0.02 ± 0.08, and glaciological bias −0.10 ± 0.10 m w.e. yr⁻¹) or clearly demonstrate the Alaska and Southern Andes gravimetry discrepancies."
     },
     {
      "index": 3,
      "type": "image",
      "weight": 0.3,
      "score": 2,
      "reasoning": "This is Mode A because the target requires quantitative comparison of observations with scenario-based model projections. The agent provides an observational cumulative series to 2023, but none of its figures include future projections, emission scenarios, projection envelopes, the 2040 exceedance comparison, or 2100 losses; thus the target visual and criterion are essentially absent."
     }
    ],
